<h3 id="punjabi" name="punjabi"><a href="punjabi">Punjabi Language</a></h3>
<p>Two scripts are used for Punjabi writing - Gurmukhi and Shahmukhi. The Gurmukhi script is used by Sikhs and Hindus in India, while the Shahmukhi script is used by Muslim Punjabis in Pakistan. Literature in Punjabi language is published in India and Pakistan and in many countries of Europe, North America and South East Asia, wherever the Punjabi diaspora is inhabited in large numbers.That is why we have created <strong> Punjabi Typing tutor </strong> to learn Punjabi language and <strong>English to Punjabi Converter </strong> to type in Punjabi write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="hindi" name="hindi"><a href="hindi">Hindi Language</a></h3>
<p>Hindi is the major language of India. Linguistically and in its everyday spoken form Hindi is virtually just like Urdu, which is that the national language of Pakistan. The two languages are often jointly mentioned as Hindustani or Hindu-Urdu. Whereas Urdu is written during a sort of Arabic script, Hindi is written left to right during a script called Devangari. That is why we have created <strong>Hindi Typing tutor </strong> to learn Hindi language and <strong>English to Hindi Converter </strong> to type in Hindi write in English as you speak.</p>

<h3 id="english" name="english"><a href="english">English Language</a></h3>
<p>The word 'English' is derived from the English, the speech of the Angels - one of the five Germanic tribes that invaded England during the fifth century. English is the mother tongue of many countries, including Australia, Canada, New Zealand, the United Kingdom and its many former colonies, and the United States, and is the second language of many multilingual countries, including India, Singapore, and Philippines.That is why we have created <strong>English Typing tutor </strong> to learn English language and <strong>English to English Converter </strong> to type in English write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="bengali" name="bengali"><a href="bengali">Bengali Language</a></h3>
<p>Bengali is the national language of Bangladesh where it is spoken by 106 million as first language and by 20 million speakers as second language. In India, it is the constitutional provincial language in the states of West Bengal, Tripura and Assam.That is why we have created <strong>Bengali Typing tutor </strong> to learn Bengali language and <strong>English to Bengali Converter </strong> to type in Bengali write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="gujarati" name="gujarati"><a href="gujarati">Gujarati Language</a></h3>
<p>Gujarati is an Indo-Aryan language spoken by approximately 46 million people in Gujarat and other state and contries. That is why we have created <strong>Gujarati Typing tutor </strong> to learn Gujarati language and <strong>English to Gujarati Converter </strong> to type in Gujarati write in English as you speak.</p>
  
<h3 id="malayalam" name="malayalam"><a href="malayalam">Malayalam Language</a></h3>
<p>Malayalam is not to be confused with Malay, the language spoken in Malaysia. Malayalam is one among the 22 official languages and 14 regional languages of India. It is spoken by 38 million people, mainly within the state of Kerala and within the Lacadive Islands in southern India. It is also spoken in Bahrain, Fiji, Israel, Malaysia, Qatar, Singapore, United Arab Emirates and the United Kingdom.That is why we have created <strong>Malayalam Typing tutor </strong> to learn Malayalam language and <strong>English to Malayalam Converter </strong> to type in Malayalam write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="marathi" name="marathi"><a href="marathi">Marathi Language</a></h3>
<p>Marathi (also referred to as Maharashtri) may be a member of the Indo-Aryan branch of the Indo-European family. It has a deep connection with Hindi and Punjabi. It is spoken by 72 million people as a primary language and by another 3 million people as a second language in India, mainly within the state of Maharashtra. Map of South Africa: India is the fourth largest language in India. Outside India, it is spoken in Israel and Mauritius (Ethnologia).That is why we have created <strong>Marathi Typing tutor </strong> to learn Marathi language and <strong>English to Marathi Converter </strong> to type in Marathi write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="odia-oriya" name="odia-oriya"><a href="odia-oriya">Odia (Oriya) Language</a></h3>
<p>Oriya, also known as Odisha, is a member of the Indo-Aryan branch of the Indo-European language family. It is spoken as the first language by 32.1 million people, most of whom live in the Indian state of Odisha, although there are also Orissa cartographic Oriya-speaking populations in West Bengal, Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh and Andhra Pradesh (Ethnologia).That is why we have created <strong>Odia (Oriya) Typing tutor </strong> to learn Odia (Oriya) language and <strong>English to Odia (Oriya) Converter </strong> to type in Odia (Oriya) write in English as you speak.</p>
    
<h3 id="tamil" name="tamil"><a href="tamil">Tamil Language</a></h3>
<p>Tamil belongs to the southern branch of the Dravidian language family, which has been spoken in southern India and northeastern Sri Lanka since prehistoric times. It is spoken as a language by 61.5 million people in India, mainly in Tamil Nadu and neighboring states, and in northeastern Sri Lanka , also as by 8 million second-language speakers (Ethnologues).That is why we have created <strong>Tamil Typing tutor </strong> to learn Tamil language and <strong>English to Tamil Converter </strong> to type in Tamil write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="telugu" name="telugu"><a href="telugu">Telugu Language</a></h3>
<p>Telugu belongs to the south central branch of the Dravidian language family. It is spoken by 74 million people as a first language and by 5 million people as a second language in India, mainly in Andra Pradesh (2001 census). It is also spoken in Bahrain, Fiji, Malaysia, Mauritius, United States, Singapore, United Kingdom and United Arab Emirates (Ethnolog).That is why we have created <strong>Telugu Typing tutor </strong> to learn Telugu language and <strong>English to Telugu Converter </strong> to type in Telugu write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="nepali" name="nepali"><a href="nepali">Nepali Language</a></h3>
<p>Nepali, a member of the Indo-Aryan branch of the Indo-European language family, is a macroleange spoken by 12,300,000 in Nepal (2011 census), 2,870,000 in India (2001 census) and 156,000 in Bhutan. Nepali speakers have a worldwide population of 15,360,100. The language is also called East Pahari, Gorkhali, Gorkhali, Khaskura, Nepali and Parbat.That is why we have created <strong>Nepali Typing tutor </strong> to learn Nepali language and <strong>English to Nepali Converter </strong> to type in Nepali write in English as you speak.</p>
 
<h3 id="kannada" name="kannada"><a href="kannada">Kannada Language</a></h3>
<p>Kannada, also known as Kanares or Canari, belongs to the southern branch of the Dravidian language family. It is spoken by 38 million people as a primary language and as a second language by 9 million people in southern India, mainly within the state of Karnataka. It is also spoken in neighboring states of Andhra Pradesh, Tamil Nadu and Maharashtra. It is estimated that it is spoken by over 44 million people worldwide, including those who speak it as a second language (Ethnologue).That is why we have created <strong>Kannada Typing tutor </strong> to learn Kannada language and <strong>English to Kannada Converter </strong> to type in Kannada write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="sanskrit" name="sanskrit"><a href="sanskrit">Sanskrit Language</a></h3>
<p>Sanskrit, which means 'complete' or 'refined', is the oldest, if not the oldest, of all ancient human languages. The oldest form of Sanskrit is Vedic Sanskrit which dates back to the 2nd millennium BC. , Known as 'mother of all languages', Sanskrit is the principal classical language of the Indian subcontinent and one of the 22 official languages &ZeroWidthSpace;&ZeroWidthSpace;of India.That is why we have created <strong>Sanskrit Typing tutor </strong> to learn Sanskrit language and <strong>English to Sanskrit Converter </strong> to type in Sanskrit write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="amharic" name="amharic"><a href="amharic">Amharic Language</a></h3>
<p>Amharic also referred to as Abyssinian, Amarigna, Amarinaya, Amhara, Ethiopia, belongs to the Semitic branch of the Afro-Asian language family. Amharic has more than 21.6 million speakers of 22 million first-language speakers and 4 million second-language speakers worldwide in Ethiopia (Ethnologia).That is why we have created <strong>Amharic Typing tutor </strong> to learn Amharic language and <strong>English to Amharic Converter </strong> to type in Amharic write in English as you speak.</p>
   
<h3 id="arabic" name="arabic"><a href="arabic">Arabic Language</a></h3>
<p>Levantine Spoken Arabic is a generic term covering a continuation of dialects spoken along the eastern Mediterranean coast of Algeria, Syria, Lebanon, Jordan, Palestine, and Israel. Levantine Arabic speakers around the world have a population of around 20 million people, many of whom are migrants from countries where it is spoken.That is why we have created <strong>Arabic Typing tutor </strong> to learn Arabic language and <strong>English to Arabic Converter </strong> to type in Arabic write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="greek" name="greek"><a href="greek">Greek Language</a></h3>
<p>Greek is one of the major civilizations and one of the largest literary languages &ZeroWidthSpace;&ZeroWidthSpace;in the world, forming its own independent branch of the Indo-European language family and has no close living relatives. Of all the surviving Indo-European languages, it is most closely related to Greece. It is spoken in the southern Balkans from the early part of the second millennium BCE and has a documented history dating back to 3,500 years, the longest record of an Indo-European language.That is why we have created <strong>Greek Typing tutor </strong> to learn Greek language and <strong>English to Greek Converter </strong> to type in Greek write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="persian" name="persian"><a href="persian">Persian Language</a></h3>
<p>Persian, Fārsi, is a member of the Indo-Iranian branch of the Indo-European language family. It is a macrolanguage spoken by an estimated 110 million people worldwide, primarily in Iran, Afghanistan, and Tajikistan. The language is known by several names. Persian is the more widely used name of the language in English, from Latin Persia, from Greek Persis. Pars is called Fars in Arabic which lacks the sound [p]. Dari is the local name used for Persian in Afghanistan. Tajik (Tajiki) is the local name used for Persian in Tajikistan.That is why we have created <strong>Persian Typing tutor </strong> to learn Persian language and <strong>English to Persian Converter </strong> to type in Persian write in English as you speak.</p>
  
<h3 id="russian" name="russian"><a href="russian">Russian Language</a></h3>
<p>Russian belongs to the Eastern Slavic group of the Slavic branch of the Indo-European language family. It is the largest of the Slavic languages. Its closest relatives are Belarusian and Ukrainian. Russian is mainly spoken by older people in the Russian Federation and in other countries that were once part of the Soviet Union, as well as in Eastern Europe. According to the 2010 census, Russians had 137 million speakers in the Russian Federation, and 166 million (ethnologues) worldwide. In addition, Canada, China, Finland, Germany, Greece, India, Israel and the U.S. Russian is spoken in. It is one among the ten most spoken languages within the world.That is why we have created <strong>Russian Typing tutor </strong> to learn Russian language and <strong>English to Russian Converter </strong> to type in Russian write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="serbian" name="serbian"><a href="serbian">Serbian Language</a></h3>
<p>Serbian belongs to the South Slavic group of the Slavic branch of the Indo-European language family. Although the term ‘Serbo-Croatian’ fell out of use, it remains the center of controversy due to its historical, cultural and political assumptions and lack of agreement in defining ‘language meanings’. Suffice it to say that these languages &ZeroWidthSpace;&ZeroWidthSpace;are to a large extent political artifacts rather than linguistic decisions.That is why we have created <strong>Serbian Typing tutor </strong> to learn Serbian language and <strong>English to Serbian Converter </strong> to type in Serbian write in English as you speak.</p>
<h3 id="sinhala-sinhalese" name="sinhala-sinhalese"><a href="sinhala-sinhalese">Sinhala (Sinhalese) Language</a></h3>
